From 74757e75d0a02cc4a15f5f1899b216373ed65224 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Langley <davidl@element.io>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 17:26:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 01/11] Build the search index on wasm (spike)

- matrix-sdk-search: on wasm, tantivy without mmap or zstd and with its
  `single-threaded` feature; the on-disk/encrypted index builders are
  gated out, so only in-memory indexes exist there.
- matrix-sdk: creating an on-disk search index store errors on wasm.
- A wasm-bindgen test exercises the in-memory index end to end (add,
  commit, search, merge, remove, edit, pagination) and prints timings.

Spike-only: the workspace patches tantivy and `symlink` to local paths
(tantivy -> the `single-threaded` fork; `symlink` -> a shim, because
tracing-appender 0.2.5 pulls it in and it has no wasm support).
